<!--META-DATA
{
	"tags": ["dice", "poker", "reroll-policy", "function", "selection-mask", "helper-compatibility"]
}
-->

<statement>
	<p>
		<pf>reroll_base</pf> (matches the earlier dealer policy, formerly <pf>get_dealer_reroll</pf>) is a practical one-pass rule: keep straights; if all dice are singles (no repeats), reroll just the first die to chase improvements; otherwise, reroll all singles using <pf>reroll_singles</pf>.
	</p>

	<tabular valign="top" halign="right" top="minor">
		<col width="12%"/>
		<col width="88%" halign="left"/>

		<row>
			<cell><p>Inputs:</p></cell>
			<cell>
				<p><pf>roll</pf> (1x5) integer — current dice (faces 1–6). Preferably sorted by rank.</p>
				<p><pf>counts</pf> (1x6) integer — face counts from <pf>get_face_counts</pf>.</p>
			</cell>
		</row>

		<row bottom="minor">
			<cell><p>Output:</p></cell>
			<cell><p><pf>sel</pf> (1x5) logical — <q>true</q> for dice to reroll, per the rule set below.</p></cell>
		</row>

		<row>
			<cell><p>Decision rule:</p></cell>
			<cell>
				<p>▸ If the hand is a straight (detected by <pf>is_straight(roll,counts)</pf>): keep all dice (<pf>sel = false(1,5)</pf>).</p>
				<p>▸ Else if all dice are singles (<pf>all(counts(roll) == 1)</pf>): reroll only the first die (<pf>sel(1) = true</pf>).</p>
				<p>▸ Else: call <pf>reroll_singles(roll,counts)</pf> to reroll all singletons and keep any pairs-or-better.</p>
			</cell>
		</row>

		<row bottom="minor">
			<cell><p>Helpers:</p></cell>
			<cell><p><pf>is_straight</pf>, <pf>reroll_singles</pf>, <pf>get_face_counts</pf>, <pf>sort_by_rank</pf></p></cell>
		</row>
	</tabular>

	<p>
		Example:
		<program>
			<code>
				roll   = [2 2 3 5 6];
				counts = get_face_counts(roll);
				roll   = sort_by_rank(roll, counts);
				sel = reroll_base(roll, counts)
				% Rerolls singles (3,5,6): sel ≈ [0 1 1 1 0]  (ordering depends on sort_by_rank)
			</code>
		</program>
	</p>
</statement>
